From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 07:44:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon/reclaim: remove damon_call() ctx NULL check

It is handled by damon_call() itself now.

Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 mm/damon/reclaim.c | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/damon/reclaim.c b/mm/damon/reclaim.c
index 09e941d75f67d..42a2c9cb13431 100644
--- a/mm/damon/reclaim.c
+++ b/mm/damon/reclaim.c
@@ -291,13 +291,6 @@ static int damon_reclaim_commit_inputs_store(const char *val,
 	if (!commit_inputs_request)
 		return 0;
 
-	/*
-	 * Skip damon_call() if ctx is not initialized to avoid
-	 * NULL pointer dereference.
-	 */
-	if (!ctx)
-		return -EINVAL;
-
 	err = damon_call(ctx, &control);
 
 	return err ? err : control.return_code;
-- 
2.47.3

